+ * to the non-secure side; the secure side -- a machine with no EL3, where EL1 and the firmware are
+ * both secure -- sees only Group 0. An interrupt marked with the other group is never delivered,
+ * but with the level of the timer still asserted it keeps the line up, so the handler is entered
+ * for ever and acknowledges a spurious interrupt each time.
+ */
